      "description": "Ebb tide. Each of the pillars of the Tay Road Bridge creating a powerful swirl of water as the ebbing tide empties the upper Firth of Tay through it, in addition to the flow of the river Tay itself. The River Tay is the largest volume river in Scotland. With a catchment area of nearly 5,000 square kilometres the average daily flow of river water alone through the road bridge is well over 200 cubic metres per second (cumecs). (As a comparison, the Severn's average flow is not much more than 100 cumecs.)",
